@flexiarg snatch/promote-the-remedy-before-the-exit
@title Promote the Remedy Before the Exit
@audience policy authors
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/have-a-temperament
@see-also snatch/consult-the-remedy-before-exiting snatch/revert-then-invert

! conclusion: The remedy-first temperament raises the arrangement's remedies above the exit rule while a breach stands, instead of dropping them.

  + context: **Policy grain.** Operand: the precedence field; membership is left
    alone. This is the cascade-level sibling of
    `snatch/consult-the-remedy-before-exiting`, which says something adjacent at
    play grain and whose THEN is compiled down to a move in the harness —
    `{:act :denounce :size (:seized s)}`, `checks/playout_snatch.clj:61-64`.

  + IF:
    A breach has been recorded and the arrangement supplies a response — a mark,
    an adjudicator, a channel.

  + HOWEVER:
    Remedies sit low in a hand-authored order because they are rarely
    applicable, and on the one round where they do become applicable "rarely" is
    the wrong reason to be consulted late. Nothing inside a pattern can say when
    that pattern should move: specificity fails here, because the pattern that
    must be consulted first has the fewest conjuncts of any acting one
    (`p4ng/app-snatch.tex:117-126`).

  + THEN:
    Emit a precedence edit that promotes the applicable remedy patterns above
    the exit rule for as long as the breach stands, and drop the edit when it no
    longer does. Record the edit on the cascade with the run.

  + BECAUSE:
    A temperament can say "consult the remedy first" once, as a fact about the
    order, instead of every play-grain pattern carrying its own clause about
    when it deserves to be reached. Availability is not use, and what makes the
    remedy available in the ordering is exactly a precedence decision.
    + evidence: the one re-wiring the harness records is a precedence edit of
      this exact shape and of no other kind — `exchange-first-overrides` moves a
      single id to 0 (`checks/playout_snatch.clj:165`) — so the runner already
      implements the operation this temperament needs. What it has never been
      asked to move is a remedy.
